WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.817
llama.cpp is a lightweight local inference project for running large language models on personal computers, workstations, servers, and homelabs.

00:00:09.817 --> 00:00:17.044
It is popular because it makes local model execution practical without requiring a large managed platform.

00:00:17.044 --> 00:00:26.521
A user can load a compatible model file, send prompts to the runtime, and experiment with language model behavior on hardware they control.

00:00:26.521 --> 00:00:30.338
Local inference is different from using a hosted AI API.

00:00:30.338 --> 00:00:37.906
With a hosted service, the provider operates the model, runtime, scaling layer, and much of the infrastructure.

00:00:37.906 --> 00:00:46.224
With llama.cpp, the user controls the model file, runtime version, hardware, performance settings, and deployment pattern.

00:00:46.224 --> 00:00:55.973
That control can improve privacy, support offline workflows, reduce dependency on external services, and make experimentation more transparent.

00:00:55.973 --> 00:01:01.291
llama.cpp is closely associated with GGUF model files and local model serving.

00:01:01.291 --> 00:01:07.222
GGUF packages model weights and metadata in a format that compatible runtimes can load.

00:01:07.222 --> 00:01:15.608
llama.cpp can run models interactively, expose local server endpoints, and act as a foundation for web UIs or applications.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:20.789
The file, runtime, prompt formatting, and hardware all have to fit together.

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:23.584
It helps to separate three levels of use.

00:01:23.584 --> 00:01:28.084
Running a model means loading it and getting output from a prompt.

00:01:28.084 --> 00:01:33.947
Serving a model means making that inference available through an API or local service.

00:01:33.947 --> 00:01:43.628
Building an application means wrapping that service with user workflows, data handling, access control, logging, and reliability expectations.

00:01:43.628 --> 00:01:51.468
Getting started with llama.cpp is about learning all three levels without losing sight of repeatability and safety.
